  "method": "Paired gene-expression and feature-library processing for A375 5-prime CRISPR with Reverse strand, and MSK ES GEX plus PolyIII and LARRY with Forward strand. MSK retains native gzip, GeneFull-only counting, no BAM, and the opt-in dominant LARRY caller disabled. The already validated cold-NVMe P02 execution is carried into the full campaign without a duplicate run. Its Cell Ranger reference time is the sum of the two retained reference workflows. Canonical feature-call and feature-UMI comparisons use the recorded thresholds, with aligned feature MEX counts additionally recorded. The corrected 1.9.5 tag was built with the accepted benchmark recipe and one SHA256-identified binary was used everywhere. Scientific arguments, input formats, reference content, hash caches, and caller settings were preserved. Each arm ran once on a quiet host, with fresh outputs and a fatal cold-cache preflight. All input, reference, output, temporary and spill locations were checked against the intended storage. Comparator outputs and times were retained; no comparator was rerun. Completion, executed-command identity, the 1.30 maximum timing ratio, and canonical correlation/cell-call tolerances were checked before scheduling the next arm. Byte equality is a recorded diagnostic rather than an acceptance gate.",
